    <h2>2. Post-Synthesis 7nm Gate Boot, De Novo Binders &amp; Zero-Linux <code>HyperOS</code></h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Metacircular <code>cub2silicon</code> on 6,342 Synthesized 7nm CMOS Gates (<code>cub2silicon-boot-certs</code>, <code>export-hypertensor-soc</code>):</strong> Compiles higher-order $\lambda$-application, <code>DUP</code> sharing, §4.5 face-guarded pruning, 1-pass <code>FlashAttention</code>, and §4.5 MoE expert routing into 32-bit boot frames, synthesized via <strong>Yosys 0.33 + Berkeley ABC</strong> onto <strong>6,342 physical 7nm CMOS standard cells</strong> (<code>2,189 NAND2</code>, <code>1,465 NOR2</code>, <code>822 XOR2</code>, <code>758 INV</code>, <code>686 MUX2</code>, <code>422 DFF</code>) and booted bit-exact (`ans = 42` in 3 cyc; `ans = 54` in 6 cyc) in <strong>Verilator 5.020</strong> gate-level simulation.</li>
    <li><strong>Zero-Hallucination De Novo Receptor Pocket Synthesis (<code>chem/pocket-binder.hypercubical</code>):</strong> Composing directional $n_O \to \sigma^*_{NH}$ H-bond perturbation (<code>chem-hb-lagrange-id</code>) with admissible subsite lower bounds (<code>pocket-s1-lb-sound</code>) prunes <strong>60 of 64 (93.75%)</strong> combinatorial scaffolds (<code>pocket-pruned-60-of-64</code>) and certifies strict global optimality (<code>lead-binder-globally-optimal</code>, $\Delta G^* = -19$ kcal/mol, 0 clashes).</li>
    <li><strong>Bare-Metal x86-64 Ring-0 Unikernel &amp; Conserved-Credit Compute Market (<code>lib/os/hyperos.hypercubical</code>):</strong> Because type-checked processes satisfy Ring-0 fiber non-interference (<code>sip-ring0-noninterference</code>, 0 <code>CR3</code> flushes), isolation costs <strong>3.5 cycles vs. 1,945.5 cycles for a Linux syscall (551.3× lower overhead)</strong>. Emitted via <code>export-hyperos-baremetal</code>, the <strong>15 KB freestanding x86-64 kernel <code>hyperos.elf</code></strong> boots directly in <strong>QEMU 8.2.2</strong> with zero Linux/POSIX, runs all five workloads in Ring 0, settles conserved <code>PoUW</code> credit (<code>pouw-conserves-credit</code>, <code>pouw-market-cert</code>), and commits its FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 <code>store/ROOT</code> digest.</li>
  </ul>

